    <briefdescription>
<para>Representation of a single sample record. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A sample record is represented by a positive integer value, which indicates how frequently was the associated line location executed.</para>
<para>Additionally, if the associated location contains a function call, the record will hold a list of all the possible called targets. For direct calls, this will be the exact function being invoked. For indirect calls (function pointers, virtual table dispatch), this will be a list of one or more functions. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
